From b3240b4a76ed143952af45dc4550e749cf08312b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 11:36:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dadao: fix AT_PAGESZ auxv immediate overflow in crt_arch.h
 (ML-024a)

crt_arch.h synthesized the AT_PAGESZ=4096 auxv entry with
`addi rd8, rd0, 4096`, but addi's immediate field (imms12) is signed
12-bit (-2048..2047, contracts/isa/spec.md SS3.6/SS1011); 4096 does not
fit and silently wrapped to 0 instead of erroring. This left
libc.page_size==0 at runtime instead of 4096, which cascaded into a
zero-length mmap(0, 0, ...) call from both musl's lite_malloc.c bump
allocator (via its PAGE_SIZE-based req/brk arithmetic, which
underflows/zeroes when PAGE_SIZE==0) and mallocng's alloc_group()
(which reads PGSZ == libc.page_size directly; its sibling alloc_meta()
only clamps a local copy that never propagates back). QEMU's mmap
responder correctly rejects a zero-length request (-EINVAL), giving a
clean NULL from malloc(); gem5's did not, returning a non-NULL but
unbacked address that only faults (MALIGN) once actually dereferenced.

Diagnosed via targeted debug instrumentation (raw write(2,...) traces
added temporarily to lite_malloc.c and mallocng/malloc.c, then
reverted) that traced two minimal repro programs down to the exact
computed values (req=0, needed=0, mmap length=0) at each layer.

Fix: use `setzw rd8, 0, 4096` (unsigned 16-bit immediate instruction,
contracts/isa/spec.md SS607/SS617) instead, which materializes 4096
exactly. Same idiom already used in tp_probe.test/mmap_backing_probe.test
for constants >2047.

Also fixes the identical bug in tests/scripts/crt0_auxv.s and a
compensating error in tests/lit/E2E/musl_crt0_auxv.test's own
expected-value construction (both sides independently wrapped to 0,
so the AT_PAGESZ check passed vacuously despite the real value being
wrong) -- tracked in the main DADAO-0628 repo, not part of this patch.

See code-agent/tasks/ML-024a-mallocng-small-sizeclass-diagnosis.md.
---
 arch/dadao/crt_arch.h | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/dadao/crt_arch.h b/arch/dadao/crt_arch.h
index a02551f6..9d1b1f28 100644
--- a/arch/dadao/crt_arch.h
+++ b/arch/dadao/crt_arch.h
@@ -80,10 +80,17 @@ START ":\n"
 "    # [3] envp terminator = NULL (empty environment)\n"
 "    sto rd8, rb1, 24\n"
 "\n"
-"    # [4..5] AT_PAGESZ(6) = 4096\n"
+"    # [4..5] AT_PAGESZ(6) = 4096. NOTE (ML-024a): `addi` takes a signed\n"
+"    # 12-bit immediate (imms12, -2048..2047, contracts/isa/spec.md SS3.6/\n"
+"    # SS1011) -- 4096 does not fit and silently wraps to 0, which was the\n"
+"    # confirmed root cause of the mallocng/lite_malloc size-class-path\n"
+"    # gap (libc.page_size ended up 0 at runtime instead of 4096). `setzw`\n"
+"    # (SS607/SS617) takes an unsigned 16-bit immediate and can materialize\n"
+"    # 4096 exactly; this idiom is already used elsewhere for constants\n"
+"    # >2047 (tests/lit/E2E/tp_probe.test, mmap_backing_probe.test).\n"
 "    addi rd8, rd0, 6\n"
 "    sto rd8, rb1, 32\n"
-"    addi rd8, rd0, 4096\n"
+"    setzw rd8, 0, 4096\n"
 "    sto rd8, rb1, 40\n"
 "\n"
 "    # [6..7] AT_UID(11) = 0\n"
-- 
